01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Rogue is a 2007 horror film written and directed by Greg McLean.

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Starring Michael Vartan, Radha Mitchell and Sam Worthington, it follows a group of
tourists in Australia who fall prey to a 7+ metre long saltwater crocodile.

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
The film was inspired by the true story of Sweetheart, a giant male saltwater crocodile that attacked
boats in the late 1970s, although Sweetheart was never responsible for an attack on a human.

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
Rogue received positive reviews from critics, but was a commercial failure.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
It is the second and last film from Dimension Films to have the involvement of
Village Roadshow Pictures, the other being 1992's Fortress.

16
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The film explores themes of crocodile, tourist, animal
attack, based on true story, wildlife.

17
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
The tone is dark and intense.
